 "last_activity": "2019-07-09T17:02:27Z",
 "messages": [
  {
   "id": "2g_tjc5-DQAJ",
   "from": "Arthur Zhao",
   "author": "7e98b49586f8806c",
   "date": "2019-07-08T22:43:26Z",
   "subject": "cable lengh",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hi,</div><div><br></div><div>Is there a function for calculating the cable length (skeleton distance) between two given nodes on a neuron ?<br></div><div><br></div><div>Thanks!</div><div>Arthur</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "Hy8jnex_DQAJ",
   "from": "Greg Jefferis",
   "author": "7f0257cd1389289f",
   "date": "2019-07-08T23:03:55Z",
   "subject": "Re: cable lengh",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Dear Arthur,<br><br><div>Thanks for your message. For this kind of work the ngraph representation of neurons is pretty useful. There is an article on the <a href=\"https://jefferis.github.io/nat/index.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://jefferis.github.io/nat/index.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792485757824000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0YgoZqLMSCtVWEhOSghwe4\">documentation site</a> which gives an overview and worked examples </div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Is there a function for calculating the cable length (skeleton distance) between two given nodes on a neuron ?<br></div></div></blockquote><div> </div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>For your specific question, see this section of the article: </div><div><br></div><div>  <a href=\"https://jefferis.github.io/nat/articles/neurons-as-graph.html#walking-along-ngraph-objects\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://jefferis.github.io/nat/articles/neurons-as-graph.html%23walking-along-ngraph-objects&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792485757824000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1qWmwaj2fp6kwxMQOIrJmt\">https://jefferis.github.io/nat/articles/neurons-as-graph.html#walking-along-ngraph-objects</a><br></div><div><br></div><div>and in brief if you have a neuron, n</div><div><br></div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Cell07PNs</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>ng</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#008\">as</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">ngraph</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> weights</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">TRUE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>igraph</span><span style=\"color:#660\">::</span><span style=\"color:#000\">distances</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">ng</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> v</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">180</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> to</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><div><br>note that in this case node indices (i.e. values between 1 and N, the number of nodes in the neuron) are being used.</div><div><br></div><div>You can also use the CATMAID id of the vertex (arbitrary integer). In that case you need to quote the ids (because they are used as the names of the nodes in the ngraph representation).</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);background-color:rgb(250,250,250);word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">dl4</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">read</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">neurons</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">catmaid</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;glomerulus DL4 right&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#000\">ng</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#008\">as</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">ngraph</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">dl4[[1]]</span><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> weights</span><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">TRUE</span><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)</span></div><div><span style=\"color:#000\">igraph::distances(ng, v=1, to=20)<br>igraph::distances(ng, v=&#39;7737299&#39;, to=&#39;44767283&#39;)<br></span></div></code></div><div><br></div></div><div>The whole article I mention above is worth a read and you can also look at this section of the function reference</div><div><br></div><div><a href=\"https://jefferis.github.io/nat/reference/index.html#section-neurons-as-graphs-\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://jefferis.github.io/nat/reference/index.html%23section-neurons-as-graphs-&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792485757824000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3UMzdQVwU2PIEUU2bgOJ3i\">https://jefferis.github.io/nat/reference/index.html#section-neurons-as-graphs-</a><br></div><div><br></div><div>Best wishes,</div><div><br></div><div>Greg.</div><div><br></div><div><br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "SaZOQNW0DQAJ",
   "from": "Arthur Zhao",
   "author": "7e98b49586f8806c",
   "date": "2019-07-09T15:13:28Z",
   "subject": "Re: cable lengh",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Dear Greg,<div><br></div><div>Thank you for the timely answer!  This is very helpful.</div><div><br></div><div>I guess in order to obtain the physical distance (since the nodes are not evenly spaced), the best way would be first getting the shortest_path, then adding up the pairwise distances? <br><br>Best,</div><div>Arthur</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br>On Monday, July 8, 2019 at 7:03:55 PM UTC-4, Greg Jefferis wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Dear Arthur,<br><br><div>Thanks for your message. For this kind of work the ngraph representation of neurons is pretty useful. There is an article on the <a href=\"https://jefferis.github.io/nat/index.html\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://jefferis.github.io/nat/index.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792485757828000&amp;usg=AOvVaw08EGxM9qJnCYJJd2ouH9J5\">documentation site</a> which gives an overview and worked examples </div><div><br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Is there a function for calculating the cable length (skeleton distance) between two given nodes on a neuron ?<br></div></div></blockquote><div> </div></div><div>For your specific question, see this section of the article: </div><div><br></div><div>  <a href=\"https://jefferis.github.io/nat/articles/neurons-as-graph.html#walking-along-ngraph-objects\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://jefferis.github.io/nat/articles/neurons-as-graph.html%23walking-along-ngraph-objects&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792485757828000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2LE1HaUaJrk_oUuYPst_46\">https://jefferis.github.io/nat/articles/neurons-as-graph.html#walking-along-ngraph-objects</a><br></div><div><br></div><div>and in brief if you have a neuron, n</div><div><br></div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#606\">Cell07PNs</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[[</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>ng</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#008\">as</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">ngraph</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> weights</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">TRUE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>igraph</span><span style=\"color:#660\">::</span><span style=\"color:#000\">distances</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">ng</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> v</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">180</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> to</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><div><br>note that in this case node indices (i.e. values between 1 and N, the number of nodes in the neuron) are being used.</div><div><br></div><div>You can also use the CATMAID id of the vertex (arbitrary integer). In that case you need to quote the ids (because they are used as the names of the nodes in the ngraph representation).</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);background-color:rgb(250,250,250);word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">dl4</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">read</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">neurons</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">catmaid</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;glomerulus DL4 right&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#000\">ng</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#008\">as</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">ngraph</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">dl4[[1]]</span><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> weights</span><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">TRUE</span><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)</span></div><div><span style=\"color:#000\">igraph::distances(ng, v=1, to=20)<br>igraph::distances(ng, v=&#39;7737299&#39;, to=&#39;44767283&#39;)<br></span></div></code></div><div><br></div></div><div>The whole article I mention above is worth a read and you can also look at this section of the function reference</div><div><br></div><div><a href=\"https://jefferis.github.io/nat/reference/index.html#section-neurons-as-graphs-\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://jefferis.github.io/nat/reference/index.html%23section-neurons-as-graphs-&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792485757828000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2KJAxca5BFY-fRf5fL-9nB\">https://jefferis.github.io/nat/reference/index.html#section-neurons-as-graphs-</a><br></div><div><br></div><div>Best wishes,</div><div><br></div><div>Greg.</div><div><br></div><div><br></div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
